# OpenSpec first — no exceptions

**If the user asks for behavior, UI, API, data, or deployable feature work → OpenSpec BEFORE `src/**` edits.**

The rule was skipped for confirmed bookings; that was wrong. Follow this order every time.

## Required sequence

```
1. npx openspec new change <kebab-id>   (or create openspec/changes/<id>/ manually)
2. proposal.md + design.md + specs/**/spec.md + tasks.md
3. npx openspec validate <id> --strict   → must pass
4. Implement tasks; mark [x] in tasks.md
5. Tests per openspec-change-testing.mdc
6. Update docs/requirements.md PRD IDs
7. Archive when done (/opsx-archive, /opsx-sync)
```

## Hard stops

- **Do NOT** create routes, components, stores, or APIs until step 3 passes.
- **Do NOT** deploy feature work that never had a validated change.
- If implementation already landed (user urgency, mistake) → **backfill** the change immediately with accurate specs and `[x]` tasks — do not skip artifacts.

## What needs OpenSpec

| Needs change | Skip |
|--------------|------|
| New pages, APIs, stores | Typos, comments only |
| UX copy / nav / flows | Formatting |
| Bug fixes changing behavior | Deps with zero behavior change |
| Deploy script behavior | User says "skip spec" |
| Cron, smoke tests for new features | |

When unsure → **create the change**.

## Validate command

```bash
npx openspec validate <change-id> --strict
```

